"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">lb</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">fresh green beans</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">trimmed</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cloves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">minced</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">sliced almonds</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">toasted, for added flavor</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Cooking Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">olive oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for sautéing</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Pepper</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-8839-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"8839\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Pot&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For blanching green beans</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Skillet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For sautéing garlic and green beans</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-8839-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-8839-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"8839\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8839-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Bring a pot of salted water to a boil. Add the green beans and blanch them for 3 minutes. Drain the beans and plunge them into ice water to stop the cooking process.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8839-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: In a large skillet, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium heat. Let it warm up while you prepare the garlic.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8839-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Add minced garlic to the skillet and sauté for 1 minute until it becomes fragrant. Be careful not to let it burn!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8839-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Add the drained green beans to the skillet. Toss them gently to coat with the garlic and olive oil.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8839-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Stir in the sliced almonds and cook for another 2–3 minutes. You want the almonds to be lightly toasted and the green beans to be tender-crisp.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-8839-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Season with salt and pepper to taste. Serve immediately and enjoy your delicious green beans garlic almonds!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-8839-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>150</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>10g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>5g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>12g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to prepare a delightful side dish with these fresh ingredients!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Green-Beans-Garlic-Almonds.webp\" alt=\"Fresh green beans, minced garlic, and toasted almonds on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-8837\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Green-Beans-Garlic-Almonds.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Ingredients-for-Green-Beans-Garlic-Almonds-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 lb fresh green beans</strong> – trimmed</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 cloves garlic</strong> – minced</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 cup sliced almonds</strong> – toasted, for added flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons olive oil</strong> – for sautéing</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt</strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Pepper</strong> – to taste</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-green-beans-garlic-almonds\"><strong>How to Make Green Beans Garlic Almonds</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful dish takes just 10 minutes to prepare and 10 minutes to cook, making it a quick and healthy side for any meal. Get ready to enjoy the crunch of almonds and the vibrant flavor of garlic with tender <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_beans\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">green beans</a>!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Preparation-Steps-for-Green-Beans-Garlic-Almonds.webp\" alt=\"A step-by-step visual guide to preparing green beans garlic almonds, showcasing the blanching, sautéing, and final presentation of the dish.\" class=\"wp-image-8838\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Preparation-Steps-for-Green-Beans-Garlic-Almonds.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Preparation-Steps-for-Green-Beans-Garlic-Almonds-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Blanch the Green Beans</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bring a pot of salted water to a boil. Add the green beans and blanch them for 3 minutes. Drain the beans and plunge them into ice water to stop the cooking process.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Heat the Olive Oil</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a large skillet, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium heat. Let it warm up while you prepare the garlic.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Sauté the Garlic</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add minced garlic to the skillet and sauté for 1 minute until it becomes fragrant. Be careful not to let it burn!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Toss in the Green Beans</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add the drained green beans to the skillet. Toss them gently to coat with the garlic and olive oil.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Add the Almonds</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Stir in the sliced almonds and cook for another 2–3 minutes. You want the almonds to be lightly toasted and the green beans to be tender-crisp.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Season and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Season with salt and pepper to taste. Serve immediately and enjoy your delicious green beans garlic almonds!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Side Dish</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot and fresh</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-green-beans-garlic-almonds\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Green beans garlic almonds</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Blanch the green beans for a vibrant color and crisp texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Toast the almonds lightly for enhanced flavor and crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use fresh garlic for a more robust taste; sauté it gently to avoid burning.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drizzle with lemon juice before serving for a refreshing zing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with adding a pinch of red pepper flakes for a subtle kick.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-green-beans-garlic-almonds\"><strong>How to Serve this Green beans garlic almonds</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve warm as a vibrant side dish to grilled chicken or fish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with quinoa or brown rice for a wholesome meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with feta or goat cheese for a creamy twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix in cherry tomatoes for a pop of color and flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Garnish with fresh herbs like parsley or basil for added freshness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy as a light lunch with a side of hummus and pita.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can easily prepare and store your Green Beans Garlic Almonds for later enjoyment:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the dish to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refrigerate for up to 3 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label the container with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool the dish completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Portion into freezer-safe bags or containers.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Remove excess air to prevent freezer burn.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 2 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in a skillet over medium heat for best texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of water or broth to prevent drying out.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat until warmed through, about 5-7 minutes.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. How do I prepare sautéed green beans with garlic and almonds?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To prepare sautéed green beans with garlic and almonds, start by trimming the ends of the green beans and rinsing them under cold water. In a skillet, heat some olive oil over medium heat, then add minced garlic and sauté until fragrant. Add the green beans and cook until they are tender-crisp, about 5-7 minutes. Finally, toss in sliced almonds and cook for an additional minute until they are lightly toasted. Season with salt and pepper to taste, and enjoy your delicious side dish!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What health benefits do green beans with garlic and almonds offer?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Green beans are low in calories and high in fiber, making them a great choice for maintaining a healthy weight. They are also rich in vitamins A, C, and K, which support immune function and bone health. Garlic is known for its potential heart health benefits and immune-boosting properties. Almonds provide healthy fats, protein, and vitamin E, contributing to overall heart health and skin wellness. Together, this dish is not only tasty but also packed with nutrients!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Can I make green beans with garlic and almonds ahead of time?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, you can prepare green beans with garlic and almonds ahead of time! You can sauté the green beans and garlic, then store them in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days. When you&#8217;re ready to serve, simply reheat them in a skillet over low heat, adding the almonds just before serving to keep them crunchy. This makes it a convenient side dish for meal prep!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. How can I adapt the green beans with garlic and almonds recipe for nut allergies?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>If you need to adapt the recipe for nut allergies, you can simply omit the almonds and replace them with sunflower seeds or pumpkin seeds for a similar crunch. Alternatively, you can use toasted breadcrumbs for added texture. The dish will still be delicious and nutritious without the nuts, so feel free to get creative with your substitutions!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to savor the delightful crunch of garlic almond green beans! This simple yet rewarding dish is perfect for any meal, bringing a burst of flavor and nostalgia to your table. So, gather your ingredients, whip it up, and enjoy the smiles it brings. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
